[PL · AUTHORITY CLARIFICATION + SIGN-IN ACTION]

Paul has clarified that this ChatGPT conversation remains the Programme Lead. The earlier “outgoing/support-only PL” transition note is SUPERSEDED. Keep one programme authority: PL here, Olumi’s Claude Code Delivery Lead for delivery sequencing, Executor for shared/hot integration.

SIGNED-IN P0 — AUTHORISED NOW
Paul authorises creation of ONE disposable invited tester account for the current staging PoC using the EXISTING Supabase Auth invite flow and built-in invite email. No new auth feature, SMTP provider, signup surface or workaround is required.

Accounts / Auth Onboarding + Olumi’s Claude Code Delivery Lead:
1) use the existing supported Supabase admin invite path;
2) send exactly one invite to Paul’s intended test email using the existing project/account context if unambiguous;
3) do NOT paste the email address, invite token, password or credentials into GitHub;
4) ensure redirect returns to the normal staging login/app path;
5) if more than one candidate email exists or the intended address is genuinely unknown, return ONE user action to Paul asking only for the target email — do not guess;
6) once invite delivery is confirmed, hand Harness the account-ready receipt.

Harness:
after Paul accepts the invite and signs in normally, run the existing ONE signed-in journey on the current served tuple:
meaningful insight → approved canonical change → stale → rerun → explained Compare → cold reload.
Record actual provider ledger evidence from Runtime/Context L1 during that same journey.

No duplicate browser journey, no shared-auth redesign, no credentials in issues.

[PTL · current correction: Canvas served / C=SCI-TEMPORAL five-P1 repair]

CANVAS #2452
CURRENT TRUTH · The earlier 19.86GiB abort receipt is historical only. It correctly describes that one failed local validation attempt, but it no longer describes product state.
GitHub now confirms #2452 CLOSED/MERGED, source923613d48b763028a9807e8c3ad87daf3257c875 → mergef6507480f53049235e1cbf1fb9cefbef0544399b. Later programme receipts establish this is included in served UI030f993c.
RULING · Do not put Canvas back into capacity-blocked/unpublished state and do not rerun its old full gate. Preserve the abort artefact as historical evidence only. Current Canvas status = MERGED/SERVED; joined acceptance remains separate.

C / SCI-TEMPORAL #2382
OWNER · existing SCI-HERO/C01a0feed retains the explicit C implementation lease for the five-P1 repair from independent review5973998055 / DL5973998182.
REMOTE BASELINE · PR2382 remains OPEN@5d2c05dda1d9970b6618693b57ec875d544cc312 against old base880b6487.
CURRENT PRODUCT BASE · served CEE3ede57eb27d525d7492866792861120ffb2ccaa2 / schemas0.75 now supersedes that as the integration baseline for finalisation.

SCOPE · Close the same five findings only:
1) generic range path must never authorise invented/unapproved range writes;
2) admission cannot depend on digit-vs-word wording;
3) capless approval must preserve raw/unit/range identity;
4) value inequality is not approval;
5) legacy/current normalisation must preserve valid range carriers without creating new range authority.
The later necessary range-only caller seams in apply-operations.ts and edit-graph.ts are within this same bounded repair only where required to prevent non-native range writes. Dedicated approved range writer remains sole range authority.

CURRENT LOCAL STATE · Treat 21 PASS / 8 FAIL as an in-progress repair checkpoint only. No source verdict or release credit until all five are closed.

FINALISATION ORDER
1) refresh/rebase the combined repair once onto current served3ede/schema0.75;
2) rerun only the exact focused producer→approval→native-writer→cold-read controls plus mutants/restore;
3) current Required + Drift/guards on the immutable descendant;
4) one independent DL final review;
5) guarded merge/deploy and actual serving verification.
No old green transfer from5d2.

EXCLUSIONS · No route/permission/Context authority, SharedData/B1/B3, SCI_CHANGE, provider/browser/full-suite scope expansion. No generic range allowlist relaxation. No extra writer or reviewer.

CLAIM LIMIT · Component green/schema-valid is insufficient; native consent/authorship, metadata integrity and cold-read persistence are part of the acceptance contract.
